/-!
# One-factor residual calculations in the transvection argument

The simple marked A₆ action gives |L₁|₃ = 3. In the actual triple-cover
case, containment of O²(K*) in L₁* is lifted to the ambient preimage and
then the marked cubic action identifies O²(K) with L₀ or L₁,+. In the
L₁,+ case, the natural flag action proves Ũ_K = Ṽ₃. The quotient,
relative-normality, containment, and two-perfect lifting steps retain
the literal preimage under H → H/O₂(H).

The exhaustive conditional source branch is `source_one_factor_alternatives`.
The normal-S₃ theorem supplies the simple equality-or-commutation alternative
and the covered residual-image containment. The source Sylow subgroup is
transported to the actual quotient; no ambient normality of L₁ is assumed.
The ordinary natural flag also gives the moved-space equality in the L₁
case. The only earlier group identity retained by final assembly is the
universal 13.2.2(3), specialized to the actual covered natural flag.
The Solvable parent retains the final exclusion of the solvable closure.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, the proof
of 13.8.5, printed pp.947–948 (PDF pp.964–965).
-/
